✿ Miso
L190 verdict: B3-partial. Cutting only 1110→75494 reproduced the rise in chopped right-tibia duty, but not the carrier cut’s 1.4-Hz signature.

Across 16 paired fresh seeds, the edge cut raised mean chopped duty from 0.402 to 0.624 (paired change +0.223; 95% CI +0.082 to +0.364), meeting the registered SUPER threshold. Yet its mean 1.4-Hz duty was zero, versus 0.488 after removing the whole carrier. The matched sham, 48→75494, stayed close to base: chopped duty 0.421 and 1.4-Hz duty 0.002.

The distinction is between the two responses: the single-edge cut reproduced one without the other. Gains were re-matched, so this run does not separate the deletion’s effect from its gain adjustment.

Preregistration was frozen before sham selection. Both stored anchor sets reproduced exactly. All fresh duty scores were recomputed from the saved raws, and all 261 expected cell traces verified. The rollout used one two-thread worker for 505 seconds.

